# Tests

## Markers

- Tests needing Hermes, Voicebox, live Gmail, or GPU Ollama on the desk machine → **`@pytest.mark.live_service`** (or documented frontend equivalent).
- Default CI / local isolated run: **`pytest -m "not live_service"`** must pass without external services.

## Offline-first

- Unit tests use in-memory or temp SQLite, mocked HTTP, and fixture files under the repo — no shop network assumptions.
- Do not hit `127.0.0.1:8642`, `:17493`, or Google APIs in unmarked tests.

## Regressions

- Every fixed production defect gets **one** targeted regression test named or commented with the matrix ID or issue — no duplicate coverage for the same bug.
- Prefer asserting observable behaviour (HTTP status, JSON fields, proof flags) over implementation details.

## Frontend

- Component tests mock fetch/SSE; WebGL-heavy bits use `--enable-unsafe-swiftshader` in headless runs (see `frontend/21-react-bits`).

## Rule budget

- `backend/tests/test_rule_budget.py` enforces `.cursor/rules/` word caps and frontmatter — update it when tiering law changes, not when product behaviour changes.

Do not weaken markers to greenwash failing live checks — fix or skip with explicit reason in the test docstring.
